config { type: "table", schema: "reportdb", name: "dash_action_items" }

/* -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   7. dash_action_items   -- SECTION 4
   -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Max 5 per page. Every item traces to a specific highlight/lowlight via
   source_item. Owner is derived from country + level_1.
   Format for rendering: '[owner] - action'.

   section = 'PERFORMANCE' : traces to a named highlight/lowlight. Max 5 per page.
   section = 'STOCK'       : traces to a named SKU list. Max 5, shown on both pages.

   =============================================================================
   2026-09-06: the prose is now written by gemini-3.5-flash, in EN and VI.
   =============================================================================

   WHAT CHANGED, AND WHAT DELIBERATELY DID NOT

   SQL still computes every FIGURE and picks every branch. The model only
   REWRITES the finished English sentence into better English and into natural
   business Vietnamese. It is never handed raw metrics and asked to do
   arithmetic, for two reasons:

     - HARD RULE 1 of the whole pipeline is that the model never computes a
       number. Letting it author the action text from raw inputs would breach
       that in the one place the board is asked to ACT on.
     - action_block is concatenated into narrative_en, and sp_dash_review_ai's
       det_numeric_ok resolves every figure in the narrative against
       facts_block + action_block. If the model authored the actions, an
       invented number would appear on BOTH sides of that check and
       SELF-AUTHORISE. The gate would pass while being wrong.

   So: SQL writes the facts, the model writes the sentence, and five
   deterministic guards below verify the model changed nothing that matters.
   Any guard failing falls the row back to the SQL text - the report always
   renders, exactly as it did before this change.

   THE FIVE GUARDS (all in the `guard` CTE, all pure SQL)

     1. numeric fidelity - every number in the model's text must already appear
        in the SQL text. Same normalisation as sp_dash_review_ai: alphanumeric
        codes stripped first so SKUs are not read as figures, leading zeros
        removed. A model that rounds 22.1 to 22 fails and falls back.
     2. code preservation - every SKU code in the SQL text must survive.
        det_sku_ok downstream requires those codes to reach narrative_vi.
     3. causal phrasing - the model's text must not match the same regex
        det_causal_claim_ok uses. roas is an efficiency ratio; "spend drove
        revenue" is a claim the attribution cannot support.
     4. diacritics - the Vietnamese must actually be Vietnamese. Mirrors
        det_diacritics_ok.
     5. non-empty and length-sane - catches the thinking-token starvation mode
        that currently has the page narratives quarantined
        (see ai-generate-thinking-token-defect.md). Hence the explicit
        thinking_budget below: this call must not repeat that failure.

   THE OWNER TAG IS ADDED IN SQL, NOT BY THE MODEL. det_owner_tags_ok counts
   '[...]' in action_block against narrative_vi. Letting the model emit the
   bracket would make that count non-deterministic, so it only ever returns the
   sentence body and SQL wraps it.

   COLUMNS: all nine existing ones keep their names and meaning. action_text is
   now the model's English (SQL on fallback); action_text_sql preserves the
   deterministic original, which is what v_dash_ai_facts_core must hash so the
   narrative cache is not busted by harmless rewording on every run.
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- */
WITH ctx AS (SELECT * FROM ${ref("dash_action_context")}), 

perf AS (
  SELECT
     c.page
    ,'PERFORMANCE' AS section
    ,c.owner
    ,CONCAT(c.country, ' / ', c.level_2, ' ',
            IF(c.item_type='HIGHLIGHT','HIGHLIGHT','LOWLIGHT')) AS source_item
    ,c.impact_vnd
    ,c.item_type
    ,ABS(c.impact_vnd) AS sort_key
    ,CASE
       -- media-readable branches: traffic_grain = 'level_3' and a click base over 100
       WHEN c.page='PAGE1_WOW' AND c.item_type='LOWLIGHT'
            AND c.media_readable AND c.traffic_verdict='SPEND_UP_CLICKS_DOWN' THEN
         FORMAT('Rework the %s buy on %s: spend %s (%s%%) returned clicks %s->%s (%s%%) and cost per click %s, alongside a %s channel decline - audit creative fatigue, audience overlap and bid caps before renewing the budget',
           IFNULL(c.attention_ads_channel,'paid'), IFNULL(c.level_3, c.level_2),
           `marine-cycle-484213-b4.reportdb.fn_fmt_money_pair`(c.attention_spend_prv, c.attention_spend_cur),
           FORMAT('%.0f', IFNULL(c.attention_spend_pct,0)*100),
           FORMAT('%d', CAST(IFNULL(c.attention_clicks_prv,0) AS INT64)), FORMAT('%d', CAST(IFNULL(c.attention_clicks_cur,0) AS INT64)),
           FORMAT('%.0f', IFNULL(c.attention_clicks_pct,0)*100),
           `marine-cycle-484213-b4.reportdb.fn_fmt_money_pair`(c.attention_cpc_prv, c.attention_cpc_cur),
           `marine-cycle-484213-b4.reportdb.fn_fmt_money`(c.impact_vnd))

       WHEN c.page='PAGE1_WOW' AND c.item_type='LOWLIGHT'
            AND c.media_readable AND c.traffic_verdict='TRAFFIC_UP_CONVERSION_DOWN' THEN
         FORMAT('Do not add budget on %s: %s clicks %s->%s (%s%%) on spend %s while NMV moved %s and bills %d->%d - review price, landing and floor conversion, and check stock cover on the top sellers first',
           IFNULL(c.level_3, c.level_2), IFNULL(c.attention_ads_channel,'paid'),
           FORMAT('%d', CAST(IFNULL(c.attention_clicks_prv,0) AS INT64)), FORMAT('%d', CAST(IFNULL(c.attention_clicks_cur,0) AS INT64)),
           FORMAT('%.0f', IFNULL(c.attention_clicks_pct,0)*100),
           `marine-cycle-484213-b4.reportdb.fn_fmt_money_pair`(c.attention_spend_prv, c.attention_spend_cur),
           `marine-cycle-484213-b4.reportdb.fn_fmt_money`(c.impact_vnd),
           c.driver_l3_bills_prv, c.driver_l3_bills_cur)

       WHEN c.page='PAGE1_WOW' AND c.item_type='LOWLIGHT'
            AND c.media_readable AND c.traffic_verdict='PAID_TRAFFIC_DOWN' THEN
         FORMAT('Recover %s delivery to %s: clicks %s->%s (%s%%) on spend %s, alongside a %s channel decline - check pacing, disapprovals and audience size before changing the offer',
           IFNULL(c.attention_ads_channel,'paid'), IFNULL(c.level_3, c.level_2),
           FORMAT('%d', CAST(IFNULL(c.attention_clicks_prv,0) AS INT64)), FORMAT('%d', CAST(IFNULL(c.attention_clicks_cur,0) AS INT64)),
           FORMAT('%.0f', IFNULL(c.attention_clicks_pct,0)*100),
           `marine-cycle-484213-b4.reportdb.fn_fmt_money_pair`(c.attention_spend_prv, c.attention_spend_cur),
           `marine-cycle-484213-b4.reportdb.fn_fmt_money`(c.impact_vnd))

       WHEN c.page='PAGE1_WOW' AND c.item_type='LOWLIGHT'
            AND c.has_site_traffic AND c.traffic_verdict='SITE_TRAFFIC_DOWN' THEN
         FORMAT('Audit the %s funnel: WEBSITE sessions %s->%s (%s%%) with bills %d->%d, alongside a %s channel decline - check indexation, page speed and the checkout path',
           IFNULL(c.level_3, c.level_2),
           FORMAT('%d', CAST(IFNULL(c.sessions_prv,0) AS INT64)), FORMAT('%d', CAST(IFNULL(c.sessions_cur,0) AS INT64)),
           FORMAT('%.0f', IFNULL(c.sessions_pct,0)*100),
           c.driver_l3_bills_prv, c.driver_l3_bills_cur,
           `marine-cycle-484213-b4.reportdb.fn_fmt_money`(c.impact_vnd))

       WHEN c.page='PAGE1_WOW' AND c.item_type='HIGHLIGHT'
            AND c.media_readable AND c.traffic_verdict='PAID_TRAFFIC_UP' THEN
         FORMAT('Hold stock cover and fulfilment capacity on %s while %s clicks run %s->%s (%s%%) at spend %s on a %s channel gain - confirm it survives past the promo window before treating it as run-rate',
           IFNULL(c.level_3,'the lead sub-channel'), IFNULL(c.attention_ads_channel,'paid'),
           FORMAT('%d', CAST(IFNULL(c.attention_clicks_prv,0) AS INT64)), FORMAT('%d', CAST(IFNULL(c.attention_clicks_cur,0) AS INT64)),
           FORMAT('%.0f', IFNULL(c.attention_clicks_pct,0)*100),
           `marine-cycle-484213-b4.reportdb.fn_fmt_money_pair`(c.attention_spend_prv, c.attention_spend_cur),
           `marine-cycle-484213-b4.reportdb.fn_fmt_money`(c.impact_vnd))

       ------------------------------------------------------------------ PAGE 1
       WHEN c.page='PAGE1_WOW' AND c.item_type='LOWLIGHT' AND c.level_1='Store'
            AND c.worst_window IS NOT NULL THEN
         -- FRAMING FIX 2026-09-07: "this week" claimed a complete week. PAGE1 is
         -- week-TO-DATE (Monday..report_date), so on any run before Sunday the
         -- phrase overstates the window. The dates are now explicit.
         FORMAT('Review floor coverage and merchandising at %s during the %s window, where bills moved %d->%d and basket moved %s (%s, the largest single loss window from %s to %s)',
           IFNULL(c.driver_level_3, c.level_2), c.worst_window,
           c.window_bills_prv, c.window_bills_cur,
           `marine-cycle-484213-b4.reportdb.fn_fmt_money_pair`(c.window_basket_prv, c.window_basket_cur),
           `marine-cycle-484213-b4.reportdb.fn_fmt_money`(c.worst_window_delta),
           LTRIM(FORMAT_DATE('%e/%m', c.sp_cur_start)),        -- NEW: WTD start
           LTRIM(FORMAT_DATE('%e/%m', c.sp_cur_end)))          -- NEW: WTD cutoff
       WHEN c.page='PAGE1_WOW' AND c.item_type='LOWLIGHT' AND c.level_1='Wholesales' THEN
         FORMAT('Re-contact the lapsed wholesale accounts: order count fell %d->%d (%s) even though average order value rose %s',
           c.driver_l3_bills_prv, c.driver_l3_bills_cur, `marine-cycle-484213-b4.reportdb.fn_fmt_money`(c.impact_vnd),
           `marine-cycle-484213-b4.reportdb.fn_fmt_money_pair`(c.driver_l3_basket_prv, c.driver_l3_basket_cur))
       WHEN c.page='PAGE1_WOW' AND c.item_type='LOWLIGHT' THEN
         FORMAT('Investigate %s specifically, which accounts for %s of the %s channel decline (bills %d->%d, basket %s)',
           IFNULL(c.driver_level_3,'the largest sub-channel'),
           `marine-cycle-484213-b4.reportdb.fn_fmt_money`(c.driver_level_3_delta), `marine-cycle-484213-b4.reportdb.fn_fmt_money`(c.impact_vnd),
           c.driver_l3_bills_prv, c.driver_l3_bills_cur,
           `marine-cycle-484213-b4.reportdb.fn_fmt_money_pair`(c.driver_l3_basket_prv, c.driver_l3_basket_cur))
       WHEN c.page='PAGE1_WOW' AND c.item_type='HIGHLIGHT' THEN
         FORMAT('Hold stock cover and fulfilment capacity on %s, which delivered %s of the %s channel gain on bills %d->%d - confirm it survives past the promo window',
           IFNULL(c.driver_level_3,'the lead sub-channel'),
           `marine-cycle-484213-b4.reportdb.fn_fmt_money`(c.driver_level_3_delta), `marine-cycle-484213-b4.reportdb.fn_fmt_money`(c.impact_vnd),
           c.driver_l3_bills_prv, c.driver_l3_bills_cur)
       ------------------------------------------------------------------ PAGE 2
       WHEN c.page='PAGE2_MTD' AND c.item_type='LOWLIGHT' AND c.stepup_x >= 2.5 THEN
         -- FRAMING FIX 2026-09-07: "%s/day achieved" carried no as-of date, so a
         -- partial-month rate read as a settled full-month one. Cutoff added.
         FORMAT('Re-forecast the month: closing the %s gap needs %s/day for the remaining %d days versus %s/day achieved month-to-date through %s, a %sx step-up that is unlikely to be traded out - escalate a revised number rather than a push',
           `marine-cycle-484213-b4.reportdb.fn_fmt_money`(c.impact_vnd), `marine-cycle-484213-b4.reportdb.fn_fmt_money`(c.required_daily),
           c.days_left, `marine-cycle-484213-b4.reportdb.fn_fmt_money`(c.achieved_daily),
           LTRIM(FORMAT_DATE('%e/%m', c.sp_cur_end)),          -- NEW: MTD cutoff
           FORMAT('%.1f', c.stepup_x))
       WHEN c.page='PAGE2_MTD' AND c.item_type='LOWLIGHT' THEN
         -- FRAMING FIX 2026-09-07: same as above - the achieved rate is MTD, and
         -- the sentence now says through when.
         FORMAT('Build a recovery plan to lift daily run-rate from %s achieved month-to-date through %s across the remaining %d days (%sx step-up) and close the %s gap',
           `marine-cycle-484213-b4.reportdb.fn_fmt_money_pair`(c.achieved_daily, c.required_daily),
           LTRIM(FORMAT_DATE('%e/%m', c.sp_cur_end)),          -- NEW: MTD cutoff
           c.days_left, FORMAT('%.1f', c.stepup_x), `marine-cycle-484213-b4.reportdb.fn_fmt_money`(c.impact_vnd))
       WHEN c.page='PAGE2_MTD' AND c.item_type='HIGHLIGHT' THEN
         -- FRAMING FIX 2026-09-07: cutoff and the forward window both stated, so
         -- "still required" is visibly a rate for days not yet traded.
         FORMAT('Protect the run-rate: %s/day achieved month-to-date through %s versus %s/day still required over the remaining %d days, so reallocate promo and stock support toward the channels behind plan rather than adding spend here',
           `marine-cycle-484213-b4.reportdb.fn_fmt_money`(c.achieved_daily),
           LTRIM(FORMAT_DATE('%e/%m', c.sp_cur_end)),          -- NEW: MTD cutoff
           `marine-cycle-484213-b4.reportdb.fn_fmt_money`(c.required_daily),
           c.days_left)                                        -- NEW: forward window
       ELSE NULL
     END AS action_text
  FROM ctx c
),

/* ===========================================================================
   perf_mtd_media   -- REWRITTEN 2026-09-07: forward-looking framing

   WHAT WAS WRONG

   The previous template ended:

       ... against NMV %s (%s%%) over 2026-08-01 to 2026-08-06
           - the same-period read, not the full prior month

   and those two dates were sp_prv_start / sp_prv_end - the PRIOR month's
   baseline window. The CURRENT window (sp_cur_start..sp_cur_end, i.e.
   month_start..report_date, 2026-09-01..2026-09-06) never appeared in the
   sentence at all. "over <dates>" reads as when the figures were recorded, so
   the one item on the page that is about the month still being traded was
   printed as a report on a month that closed five weeks ago. The trailing
   qualifier was the only thing holding the meaning together, and it is exactly
   what gemini-3.5-flash dropped when it rewrote the sentence:

       "Optimize TIKTOK campaigns ... recorded over 2026-08-01 to 2026-08-06."

   THE FIX, IN THREE PARTS

     1. The sentence now OPENS with the forward period - days_left and the month
        name - so the instruction is unambiguously about days not yet traded.
     2. The current window is stated as an explicit cutoff, "month-to-date
        through 6/09", instead of being left implicit.
     3. The prior window is named as what it is - "the same days last month" -
        and its dates are parenthesised, so they read as the baseline rather
        than as the recording period.

   The qualifier "- the same-period read, not the full prior month" is retired:
   "the same days last month (1/08-6/08)" says it in the sentence's own grammar,
   which is far harder for a rewrite to drop without the loss being visible.

   NOTHING NUMERIC CHANGED. Every metric expression below is byte-identical to
   the previous version. The only new substitutions are date and day-count
   formatting drawn from columns dash_action_context already publishes.

   DATE ANCHOR NOTE. days_left comes from dash_page2_mtd.data_as_of; sp_cur_end
   comes from dash_run_params.report_date. They are the same date on every run
   (verified 2026-09-06 = 2026-09-06), and the assertion in config guards it. If
   they ever drift, this sentence would say "through 6/09 ... remaining 25 days"
   while the run-rate items beside it say 24, so the assertion fails the run
   rather than shipping two different as-of dates on one page.
   ======================================================================== */
perf_mtd_media AS (
  SELECT
     c.page, 'PERFORMANCE' AS section, c.owner
    ,CONCAT(c.country, ' / ', c.level_2, ' LOWLIGHT') AS source_item
    ,c.impact_vnd, c.item_type, ABS(c.impact_vnd) * 0.5 AS sort_key
    ,FORMAT('Set the %s plan on %s for the remaining %d days of %s: month-to-date through %s, spend %s and clicks %s->%s (%s%%) against NMV %s (%s%%), vs the same days last month (%s-%s)'
       -- %1  ads channel carrying the move, from the att_up/att_down pick in
       --     dash_action_context. UNCHANGED.
       ,IFNULL(c.attention_ads_channel,'paid media')
       -- %2  the sub-channel the action lands on. UNCHANGED.
       ,IFNULL(c.level_3, c.level_2)
       -- %3  NEW - days still to trade this month. dash_page2_mtd:
       --     DATE_DIFF(LAST_DAY(month_start), data_as_of, DAY) => 24.
       --     This is what makes the sentence an instruction, not a report.
       ,c.days_left
       -- %4  NEW - month name of the CURRENT window => 'September'.
       --     sp_cur_end, never sp_prv_end: the month being traded.
       ,FORMAT_DATE('%B', c.sp_cur_end)
       -- %5  NEW - the MTD cutoff, stated explicitly => '6/09'.
       --     sp_cur_end = mtd_end = dash_run_params.report_date.
       --     LTRIM strips the space %e pads single-digit days with.
       ,LTRIM(FORMAT_DATE('%e/%m', c.sp_cur_end))
       -- %6  paid spend, prior->current, one shared unit. UNCHANGED.
       ,`marine-cycle-484213-b4.reportdb.fn_fmt_money_pair`(c.attention_spend_prv, c.attention_spend_cur)
       -- %7  %8  clicks prior -> current on that channel. UNCHANGED.
       ,FORMAT('%d', CAST(IFNULL(c.attention_clicks_prv,0) AS INT64))
       ,FORMAT('%d', CAST(IFNULL(c.attention_clicks_cur,0) AS INT64))
       -- %9  click change, whole percent. UNCHANGED.
       ,FORMAT('%.0f', IFNULL(c.attention_clicks_pct,0)*100)
       -- %10 same-period NMV, prior->current. UNCHANGED.
       ,`marine-cycle-484213-b4.reportdb.fn_fmt_money_pair`(c.sp_nmv_prv, c.sp_nmv_cur)
       -- %11 NMV change, whole percent. UNCHANGED.
       ,FORMAT('%.0f', IFNULL(c.sp_nmv_pct,0)*100)
       -- %12 %13 THE TWO DATES THAT CAUSED THE DEFECT. Same columns as before -
       --     sp_prv_start / sp_prv_end, the prior month's same-day window - but
       --     now short-form and inside "the same days last month (...)", where
       --     they can only be read as the baseline. Previously they sat after
       --     "over", which reads as the recording period.
       ,LTRIM(FORMAT_DATE('%e/%m', c.sp_prv_start))
       ,LTRIM(FORMAT_DATE('%e/%m', c.sp_prv_end))
     ) AS action_text
  FROM ctx c
  WHERE c.page='PAGE2_MTD' AND c.item_type='LOWLIGHT' AND c.media_readable
),

traffic AS (
  SELECT
     c.page, 'PERFORMANCE' AS section, 'Data / BI Lead' AS owner
    ,CONCAT(c.country, ' / ', c.level_2, ' LOWLIGHT') AS source_item
    ,c.impact_vnd, c.item_type, ABS(c.impact_vnd) * 0.4 AS sort_key
    ,CASE
       WHEN c.level_1 = 'Store' THEN
         FORMAT('Instrument door-count footfall for %s / %s: bills moved %d->%d, and with no footfall capture in any source system a visit loss and a conversion loss still cannot be told apart on the shop floor',
           c.country, c.level_2, c.driver_l3_bills_prv, c.driver_l3_bills_cur)
       ELSE
         FORMAT('Bring %s seller-centre traffic into the pipeline for %s / %s: bills moved %d->%d and no media or session data exists for this sub-channel, so its %s move can only be read as a trade result',
           IFNULL(c.level_3,'the marketplace'), c.country, c.level_2,
           c.driver_l3_bills_prv, c.driver_l3_bills_cur,
           `marine-cycle-484213-b4.reportdb.fn_fmt_money`(c.impact_vnd))
     END AS action_text
  FROM ctx c
  WHERE c.page='PAGE1_WOW'
    AND c.item_type='LOWLIGHT'
    AND c.traffic_verdict IN ('NOT_INSTRUMENTED','MEDIA_NOT_AT_THIS_LEVEL_3','MEDIA_TOO_SMALL_TO_READ')
    AND IFNULL(c.driver_l3_bills_cur,0) < IFNULL(c.driver_l3_bills_prv,0)
),

stock AS (
  SELECT 'BOTH' AS page, 'STOCK' AS section, 'Kho/Vận Hành' AS owner,
         CONCAT('Stock list: ', list_name) AS source_item,
         rank_value AS impact_vnd, 'LOWLIGHT' AS item_type, rank_value AS sort_key,
         CASE list_name
           WHEN 'OVERSTOCK' THEN FORMAT('Put %s (%s) into a clearance or transfer plan: %d units on hand, %s weeks of cover, %s%% sell-through and %s of value tied up',
             variation_code, IFNULL(product_name,'unnamed'), CAST(units_on_hand AS INT64),
             FORMAT('%.0f', cover_weeks), FORMAT('%.0f', sell_through_rate*100), `marine-cycle-484213-b4.reportdb.fn_fmt_money`(rank_value))
           WHEN 'UNDERSTOCK' THEN FORMAT('Raise a replenishment order for %s (%s) now: only %d units left at %s weeks cover with %s%% sell-through, putting %s of four-week demand at risk',
             variation_code, IFNULL(product_name,'unnamed'), CAST(units_on_hand AS INT64),
             FORMAT('%.1f', cover_weeks), FORMAT('%.0f', sell_through_rate*100), `marine-cycle-484213-b4.reportdb.fn_fmt_money`(rank_value))
           WHEN 'DISCONTINUED' THEN FORMAT('Clear discontinued %s (%s): %d units still held at %s retail value with %s%% sell-through and no active sales plan',
             variation_code, IFNULL(product_name,'unnamed'), CAST(units_on_hand AS INT64),
             `marine-cycle-484213-b4.reportdb.fn_fmt_money`(rank_value), FORMAT('%.0f', sell_through_rate*100))
           ELSE FORMAT('Secure supply for trending %s (%s): units sold rose %d->%d week on week with %s weeks of cover remaining',
             variation_code, IFNULL(product_name,'unnamed'),
             CAST(IFNULL(units_prv,0) AS INT64), CAST(IFNULL(units_cur,0) AS INT64), FORMAT('%.1f', cover_weeks))
         END AS action_text
  FROM ${ref("dash_stock_lists")}
  WHERE rank_in_list <= 2
),

u AS (
  SELECT page, section, owner, source_item, impact_vnd, item_type, sort_key, action_text FROM perf
  WHERE action_text IS NOT NULL
  UNION ALL SELECT page, section, owner, source_item, impact_vnd, item_type, sort_key, action_text FROM perf_mtd_media
  UNION ALL SELECT page, section, owner, source_item, impact_vnd, item_type, sort_key, action_text FROM traffic
  UNION ALL SELECT page, section, owner, source_item, impact_vnd, item_type, sort_key, action_text FROM stock
),

/* the deterministic spine: exactly what this table produced before */
spine AS (
  SELECT * EXCEPT(rn, sort_key, action_text)
        ,action_text AS action_text_sql
        ,rn          AS action_no
  FROM (
    SELECT u.*, ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY page, section ORDER BY sort_key DESC) AS rn
    FROM u
  )
  WHERE rn <= 5
),

/* ===========================================================================
   The model call. One per action line - at most 13 rows, so this is a rounding
   error against ai_exec_run's 28 GB/month.

   max_output_tokens is 8192 with thinking_budget 1024. Gemini 3 counts internal
   reasoning against the output ceiling, and the page-narrative call is currently
   quarantined precisely because a 10,000 ceiling was swallowed by 9,598 thinking
   tokens, leaving the model 43 to write with. See
   ai-generate-thinking-token-defect.md. This call is sized so that cannot
   happen: the reasoning is capped and the remaining ~7,000 is far more than two
   sentences need.
   ======================================================================== */
gen AS (
  SELECT
     s.*
    ,AI.GENERATE(
       CONCAT(
'Rewrite one retail action item for a board report. Return polished English and natural Vietnamese.\n\n',
'ABSOLUTE RULES\n',
'1. Every number stays EXACTLY as written - same digits, decimals, signs and units. Never round,\n',
'   reformat, convert or drop one. Do not add a number that is not in the input.\n',
'2. Store names, platform names, channel names and product codes stay EXACTLY as written, in both\n',
'   languages. Never translate or transliterate them (Store Nguyen Trai, Emsphere, Shopee, TIKTOK,\n',
'   META, GOOGLE_ADS, V26011696, YERI DRESS).\n',
'3. Never write that spend, ads, paid media or a campaign drove, generated, delivered, produced or\n',
'   caused revenue. The attribution cannot support it. State the figures side by side instead\n',
'   ("alongside", "while").\n',
'4. Do NOT add an owner tag or any [bracket] prefix - that is added afterwards.\n',
'5. One sentence, imperative, an instruction someone can act on. Max 60 words.\n',
'6. KEEP THE TIME FRAMING. If the input is written about days STILL TO COME - "for the\n',
'   remaining N days of <month>" - the output must stay about days still to come, in BOTH\n',
'   languages. Never turn it into a past or completed period. Keep every "month-to-date\n',
'   through <date>", "for the remaining N days" and "the same days last month" phrase, and\n',
'   keep each date attached to the clause it is in. A date after "through" is the CUTOFF of\n',
'   the period being traded now; a date in "the same days last month (...)" is the BASELINE.\n',
'   Never swap them, never merge them, and never write that the figures were "recorded over"\n',
'   or "measured during" the baseline dates.\n\n',
'VIETNAMESE: natural professional retail Vietnamese with full diacritics, not a word-for-word\n',
'translation. Use standard trade vocabulary (doanh thu, hoa don, gia tri gio hang, ton kho,\n',
'ty le ban ra, chi tieu, tien do, chi phi quang cao, luot nhap, luot truy cap).\n\n',
'ACTION TO REWRITE:\n', s.action_text_sql
       ),
       connection_id => 'marine-cycle-484213-b4.asia-southeast1.agent_platform_ai',
       endpoint      => 'gemini-3.5-flash',
       model_params  => JSON '{"generation_config":{"max_output_tokens":8192,"temperature":0.3,"thinking_config":{"thinking_budget":1024}}}',
       output_schema => 'action_en STRING, action_vi STRING'
     ) AS ai
  FROM spine s
),

/* ===========================================================================
   Five deterministic guards. Nothing here trusts the model.
   ======================================================================== */
guard AS (
  SELECT
     g.* EXCEPT(ai)
    ,g.ai.action_en AS ai_en
    ,g.ai.action_vi AS ai_vi
    ,CAST(JSON_VALUE(g.ai.full_response,'$.usage_metadata.prompt_token_count')     AS INT64) AS prompt_tokens
    ,CAST(JSON_VALUE(g.ai.full_response,'$.usage_metadata.candidates_token_count') AS INT64) AS output_tokens
    ,CAST(JSON_VALUE(g.ai.full_response,'$.usage_metadata.thoughts_token_count')   AS INT64) AS thinking_tokens

    -- 1. numeric fidelity. Codes stripped first so SKUs are not read as figures,
    --    leading zeros normalised - same treatment sp_dash_review_ai applies.
    ,ARRAY(
       SELECT x FROM UNNEST(ARRAY(SELECT DISTINCT IF(LTRIM(a,'0')='','0',LTRIM(a,'0'))
         FROM UNNEST(REGEXP_EXTRACT_ALL(
           REGEXP_REPLACE(CONCAT(IFNULL(g.ai.action_en,''),' ',IFNULL(g.ai.action_vi,'')),
             r'[A-Za-z]+[0-9]+[A-Za-z0-9\-]*', ' '), r'[0-9]+(?:\.[0-9]+)?')) a)) x
       WHERE x NOT IN UNNEST(ARRAY(SELECT DISTINCT IF(LTRIM(b,'0')='','0',LTRIM(b,'0'))
         FROM UNNEST(REGEXP_EXTRACT_ALL(
           REGEXP_REPLACE(g.action_text_sql, r'[A-Za-z]+[0-9]+[A-Za-z0-9\-]*', ' '),
           r'[0-9]+(?:\.[0-9]+)?')) b))
     ) AS invented_numbers

    -- 2. every product code in the SQL text must survive into BOTH languages
    ,(SELECT LOGICAL_AND(REGEXP_CONTAINS(IFNULL(g.ai.action_en,''), code)
                     AND REGEXP_CONTAINS(IFNULL(g.ai.action_vi,''), code))
      FROM UNNEST(IFNULL(REGEXP_EXTRACT_ALL(g.action_text_sql, r'\b[A-Z][0-9]{6,}[0-9A-Z\-]*\b'), [])) code)
      IS NOT FALSE                                                        AS codes_kept

    -- 3. the same causal regex det_causal_claim_ok enforces
    ,NOT REGEXP_CONTAINS(LOWER(CONCAT(IFNULL(g.ai.action_en,''),' ',IFNULL(g.ai.action_vi,''))),
        r'\b(spend|spending|advertising|ad spend|ads|paid media|campaigns?)\b[^.]{0,40}\b(drove|driving|generated|delivered|produced|caused|resulted in)\b')
                                                                          AS causal_ok

    -- 4. the Vietnamese must actually carry diacritics
    ,REGEXP_CONTAINS(IFNULL(g.ai.action_vi,''),
      r'[àáâãèéêìíòóôõùúýăđĩũơưạảấầẩẫậắằẳẵặẹẻẽếềểễệỉịọỏốồổỗộớờởỡợụủứừửữựỳỵỷỹ]')
                                                                          AS diacritics_ok

    -- 5. non-empty and not a truncated stub
    ,LENGTH(IFNULL(g.ai.action_en,'')) >= 40 AS en_present
    ,LENGTH(IFNULL(g.ai.action_vi,'')) >= 40 AS vi_present

    -- 6. TIME FRAMING - added 2026-09-07.
    --    The PAGE2 items are instructions for days not yet traded. A model can
    --    keep every number and still invert the instruction: "for the remaining
    --    24 days" -> "over the last 24 days" passes guard 1 untouched, because
    --    24 is in both texts. Rule 1 cannot see meaning, only digits.
    --
    --    Asymmetric on purpose. English is checked POSITIVELY - the input is
    --    English, prompt rule 6 tells the model to keep the phrase, so requiring
    --    'remaining' back is safe. Vietnamese is checked NEGATIVELY, for the
    --    absence of a past-period marker, because there are several correct ways
    --    to render "remaining" (24 ngay con lai / phan con lai cua thang) and a
    --    positive list would fall perfectly good Vietnamese back to English -
    --    which is the one thing the Vietnamese report cannot afford.
    ,(NOT REGEXP_CONTAINS(LOWER(g.action_text_sql), r'\bremaining\b'))
       OR (REGEXP_CONTAINS(LOWER(IFNULL(g.ai.action_en,'')), r'\bremaining\b')
           AND NOT REGEXP_CONTAINS(LOWER(IFNULL(g.ai.action_vi,'')),
                 r'vừa qua|đã qua|trước đây|tuần qua|tháng qua|trong quá khứ'))
                                                                          AS frame_ok

    -- 7. DATE TOKENS - added 2026-09-07.
    --    Every d/mm token in the SQL sentence must survive into both languages.
    --    Guard 1 already authorises the digits 6, 9, 1 and 8, so a model that
    --    wrote "through 6/08" instead of "through 6/09" - swapping the cutoff for
    --    the baseline, which is precisely the defect being fixed - would pass
    --    numeric fidelity. This checks the tokens themselves, not their digits.
    --    Word boundaries so '6/09' does not satisfy itself from inside '16/09'.
    ,(SELECT LOGICAL_AND(REGEXP_CONTAINS(IFNULL(g.ai.action_en,''), CONCAT(r'\b', tok, r'\b'))
                     AND REGEXP_CONTAINS(IFNULL(g.ai.action_vi,''), CONCAT(r'\b', tok, r'\b')))
      FROM UNNEST(IFNULL(REGEXP_EXTRACT_ALL(g.action_text_sql, r'\b[0-9]{1,2}/[0-9]{2}\b'), [])) tok)
      IS NOT FALSE                                                        AS dates_kept
  FROM gen g
),

verdict AS (
  SELECT
     x.*
    ,ARRAY_LENGTH(x.invented_numbers) = 0 AS numbers_ok
    ,CASE
       WHEN NOT x.en_present OR NOT x.vi_present     THEN 'empty_or_truncated'
       WHEN ARRAY_LENGTH(x.invented_numbers) > 0     THEN 'invented_number'
       WHEN NOT x.codes_kept                         THEN 'code_dropped'
       WHEN NOT x.causal_ok                          THEN 'causal_claim'
       WHEN NOT x.diacritics_ok                      THEN 'no_diacritics'
       WHEN NOT x.frame_ok                           THEN 'frame_flipped'
       WHEN NOT x.dates_kept                         THEN 'date_dropped'
       ELSE 'ok'
     END                                             AS gen_status
  FROM guard x
)

SELECT
   page, section, owner, source_item, impact_vnd, item_type

   -- the model's English where it passed every guard, the SQL sentence otherwise
  ,IF(v.gen_status = 'ok', v.ai_en, v.action_text_sql)                    AS action_text
   -- Vietnamese for the report. On a guard failure this falls back to the
   -- English SQL sentence rather than NULL, so section 4 always renders
   -- something true; vi_source says which the reader is looking at.
  ,IF(v.gen_status = 'ok', v.ai_vi, v.action_text_sql)                    AS action_text_vi
  ,v.action_text_sql
  ,action_no

   -- the owner tag is wrapped here, never by the model
  ,CONCAT('[', owner, '] - ', IF(v.gen_status = 'ok', v.ai_en, v.action_text_sql)) AS action_item
  ,CONCAT('[', owner, '] - ', IF(v.gen_status = 'ok', v.ai_vi, v.action_text_sql)) AS action_item_vi

   -- provenance, so a reader can always tell what wrote the sentence in front of them
  ,v.gen_status
  ,IF(v.gen_status = 'ok', 'ai', 'sql')                                   AS text_source
  ,IF(v.gen_status = 'ok', 'ai_vi', 'en_fallback')                        AS vi_source
  ,v.numbers_ok, v.codes_kept, v.causal_ok, v.diacritics_ok, v.frame_ok, v.dates_kept
  ,v.invented_numbers
  ,'gemini-3.5-flash'                                                     AS model_endpoint
  ,v.prompt_tokens, v.output_tokens, v.thinking_tokens
  ,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP()                                                    AS generated_at
FROM verdict v